PART 10: FOOD PLANNING AND WASTAGE REDUCTION

22. Smart Food Calculator

This is the main business value of WeddingGuest.

Create a dedicated food planning section.

Automatically calculate:

- Confirmed adults.
- Confirmed children.
- Total confirmed attendees.
- Optional food buffer.
- Recommended food preparation quantity.

Example:

Confirmed adults: 180

Confirmed children: 40

Total confirmed: 220

Food buffer: 5%

Recommended food preparation: 231 plates.

Formula:

Recommended plates = Confirmed attendees × (1 + buffer percentage / 100)

Round the result up to the next whole number.

Allow hosts to change the buffer percentage.

Default buffer: 5%.

Allow a buffer of 0% to 30%.

23. Food Planning Rules

Very important:

- Only confirmed attendees should be included.
- Declined guests must not be counted.
- Pending guests must not automatically be counted as confirmed.
- Updated RSVP responses must immediately update the calculation.
- Avoid counting the same guest twice.
- Calculate separately for each wedding function.
- Allow manual adjustments by the host.

Add an optional scenario calculator:

Scenario 1: Confirmed guests only.

Scenario 2: Confirmed guests plus expected pending responses.

Scenario 3: Confirmed guests plus selected buffer.

Clearly distinguish estimates from confirmed attendance.

24. Catering Planning

Create an optional catering planner.

