PART 19: SECURITY AND VALIDATION

37. Security Requirements

- Use Firebase Authentication.
- Implement strict Firestore security rules.
- Users can only access their own wedding records.
- Guests can access only their intended public invitation and RSVP functionality.
- Use cryptographically secure random invitation tokens.
- Do not expose guest lists publicly.
- Do not expose phone numbers to other guests.
- Validate all input on the backend.
- Protect against unauthorized database updates.
- Rate-limit public RSVP endpoints where possible.
- Protect against duplicate submissions.
- Avoid exposing private wedding information through URLs.
- Provide secure data deletion.

Never trust frontend-only validation for sensitive operations.

